```{r, include = FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(
  collapse = TRUE,
  comment = "#>",
  dpi = 300,
  message = FALSE,
  warning = FALSE,
  cache = TRUE
)

options(dplyr.width = Inf)
```

Prior to `mermaidr` version 2.0.0, you had the option to access environmental covariates along with data from MERMAID Collect directly in `mermaidr`. These covariates have been centralized into the *MERMAID covariates* platform, and the ability to access them has been moved to a dedicated package, `mermaidrcovariates`, and removed from `mermaidr`.

The newly released *MERMAID covariates* platform is a centralized, regularly updated catalogue of remote-sensing datasets — climate, environmental, and social — which are normalized so they can be paired directly with MERMAID survey locations. You can browse the full catalogue at [mermaid.prescient.earth](https://mermaid.prescient.earth/), and access the data programmatically through `mermaidrcovariates`, a companion to `mermaidr`, used throughout this vignette.

For full usage details of `mermaidrcovariates`, please visit its [website](https://data-mermaid.github.io/mermaidr-covariates/).

This vignette will specifically walk through accessing the environmental covariates that were previously included alongside data accessed from `mermaidr`. Note that not all datasets were migrated:

